   "tap_sector (Technology row)": "the donut's centre changes from 'TOTAL $198.8K 42 holdings' to 'TECHNOLOGY 57% S&P 500: 39%', every other sector dims in both rings and in the list, and the row opens to its 18 holdings, two of them 'via QQQ 3.5%' and 'via VOO 3.4%' (the part held inside those funds); instant re-render, no animation",
   "tap_ring (the blue Communication Services segment of the outer ring)": "the selection moves to that sector: the centre reads 'COMMUNICATION S... 8.2% S&P 500: 9.5%', only the blue segments stay lit, the Technology row closes and the Communication Services row opens (GOOGL 3.1%, META 2.3%, NFLX 1.2%, via VOO 0.8%, via QQQ 0.8%); instant",
   "tap_restore (the same segment again)": "deselects: the donut is fully lit again with 'TOTAL $198.8K', every row closed (the take's first state, so the video loops); instant",
   "explored, not recorded": "tapping an open sector row closes it and restores the first state; an industry-group row ('Chip companies') opens its holdings list but does not change the donut; the expand arrow is part of the row (same tap)"
